   Combinatorially the Bernoulli numbers are an inclusion exclusion, where the sum is taken
over all words of length n with k distinct letters, and normalized by k + 1.

    We are interested in an extension to the Bernoulli numbers defined by Kaneko [2], [12],
[13]. They are in terms of infinite series, and although we will not use this form it is presented
for historical context. Kaneko begins with an alternate definition of the Bernoulli numbers
